> SJ71 Limited is a real estate development company with a special commitment to innovation and community building. Guided by the vision of entrepreneur MD Tarekh Rana, SJ71 is creating a portfolio of multi-use commercial/residential properties and businesses that are enhancing the urban fabric and diversity of Durham Region.
From its humble beginnings investing strategically in properties and buildings showing great potential in Durham Region, SJ71 has developed a planning and construction methodology founded on the innovative use of construction technology, energy efficient and sustainable materials and state of the art design.
Responding to the identified need for conference, meeting and event spaces in the area, SJ71 is contributing to the development of new cultural diversity that has made Canada the great success that it is.
SJ71 is committed to giving back to neighbourhoods that support its investment and development activities by sharing our planning and development expertise with community organizations.
The Old Pump House is SJ71’s first foray into heritage conservation.
The project involves restoring a 2700 square foot stone heritage building and adding another 8000 square feet in a style and using materials that are consistent with the historical character of the original. The building will house a restaurant/bar and meeting facilities, serving local Whitby residents and businesses while also drawing tourists to the Whitby waterfront. The Old Pump Station will complement existing waterfront attractions like the lighthouse, marina and Heydenshore Pavilion.
The character of the original 1904 pump house will be maintained through restoration of the stone walls, windows and roof. The addition will match in both materials and design. When combined with outdoor patios, the addition will increase the site’s utility and take advantage of lakeside views.
Green roofs and energy efficient fixtures throughout will contribute to sustainability. Exterior landscaping, walkways & bike paths, warming huts and cobblestone parking will complete the waterfront experience.
